otype is a well-defined, immunologically specific cell type—CD4+ αβ T cells with a memory differentiation state—central to adaptive immunity and immune memory. The concept is precise in scope, excluding naïve, CD8+, and γδ T cells, and is grounded in molecular and functional immunology.
