ation of biological process" is a technical, mechanism-specific synonym used almost exclusively in scientific and clinical-genetic contexts. It reflects a molecular-level reduction in the expression or activity of a biological process, typically observed in gene expression studies or molecular diagnostics. It is not a layperson term and is not used in patient communication. Its primary users are **healthcare professionals and researchers**, making them the dominant group in real-world application.
