*Conclusion:**   "Retinal dystrophy" is a high-level, clinically relevant HPO concept denoting a genetically determined, progressive degeneration of retinal tissue, primarily affecting photoreceptors and/or RPE. It serves as a parent term for more specific retinal degenerative conditions and is used to describe a broad category of inherited retinal diseases with shared pathological and clinical features.
