ific, measurable anatomical abnormality characterized by an elongated horizontal eye opening, primarily relevant in the context of congenital craniofacial dysmorphology and genetic syndromes. It is a well-defined morphological phenotype with clear anatomical boundaries and clinical utility in differential diagnosis.
