f teeth" is a precise, developmentally focused phenotype describing a delay in the emergence of teeth into the oral cavity, distinct from other dental developmental abnormalities. It is contextually tied to normal growth and maturation timelines and is used to identify underlying genetic, metabolic, or systemic conditions.
