*   "Abnormal diaphysis morphology" is a precise, anatomically focused phenotype describing structural deviations in the shaft of long bones, independent of the underlying cause. It is a high-level phenotypic descriptor used to capture morphological abnormalities in the diaphysis, with broad relevance across developmental, genetic, and metabolic bone disorders.
