mb bud development, particularly in the specification and segmentation of digit identity and number.  **Conclusion:**   "Postaxial hand polydactyly" is a well-defined, anatomically specific congenital phenotype involving the presence of one or more extra digits on the little finger side of the hand. It is distinct from other forms of polydactyly by location (postaxial), structure (hand), and developmental origin. The concept is broad enough to include various morphological variants of postaxial duplication but excludes involvement of other limbs or digit sides.
