otes a structural anomaly of the corticospinal motor pathways, specifically involving their form, size, or organization. It is a precise, anatomically defined phenotype relevant to neurodevelopmental and neurodegenerative disorders, with clear boundaries in terms of affected structure and exclusion of functional or non-pyramidal tract abnormalities.
