 of hair" refers to the early loss of hair pigmentation due to premature melanocyte dysfunction in hair follicles, occurring significantly earlier than normal aging. It is a distinct clinical phenotype with specific anatomical (hair follicle), physiological (melanin production), and temporal (premature onset) criteria, and is used in genetic and clinical diagnostics to identify underlying conditions.
