herited metabolic disorders and renal tubular diseases. It is often detected via urine amino acid profiling and may be associated with systemic manifestations (e.g., kidney stones, neurological symptoms, growth retardation) depending on the underlying cause.  **Conclusion:**   "Aminoaciduria" is a precise, clinically relevant phenotype denoting pathological amino acid excretion in urine due to defects in renal tubular reabsorption or systemic amino acid metabolism. It serves as a key diagnostic indicator in inherited metabolic and renal tubular disorders.
