 focal hyperhidrosis.   - **Parent Concepts:** "Hyperhidrosis" (HP:0000951), "Abnormality of the skin" (HP:0000952), and "Abnormality of the integument" (HP:0000953), indicating it is a subtype of generalized hyperhidrosis with a localized manifestation.   - **Child Concepts:** May include "Primary palmar hyperhidrosis" (if distinguished from secondary causes), reinforcing the focus on localized, idiopathic sweating.  **Conclusion:**   The HPO concept "Palmar hyperhidrosis" describes a specific, localized form of pathological excessive sweating confined to the palms, with clear anatomical and physiological boundaries. It is distinct from generalized or secondary hyperhidrosis and is clinically relevant in dermatology and neurology.
