olving transcription factors like SOX9 or RUNX2).    **Conclusion:**   "Abnormal tarsal ossification" refers to a specific developmental defect in the ossification of the tarsal bones, encompassing any deviation from normal timing, pattern, or extent of bone formation in this anatomical region. It is a phenotype rooted in skeletal development and is distinct from broader skeletal abnormalities or non-ossification-related foot malformations.
