gical Position:** As a child of broader terms such as "abnormality of the hand" and "abnormality of the phalanx," this concept is specific to the thumb and the complete bony duplication, distinguishing it from other forms of phalangeal malformations (e.g., hypoplasia, fusion, or agenesis).  **Conclusion:**   The phenotype is a rare, specific congenital anomaly involving the complete duplication of a single phalanx in the thumb, with clear anatomical and developmental boundaries. It is distinct from other digit duplications or partial phalangeal abnormalities.
