usion:**   "Abnormal 5th metacarpal morphology" refers to any non-standard structural form of the fifth metacarpal bone, encompassing a wide range of congenital or acquired shape abnormalities. It is a precise anatomical descriptor with broad phenotypic scope, primarily relevant in the context of skeletal development and genetic syndromes involving hand malformations.
