tological Positioning:** As a child of "contracture of the toe" (HP:0001777) and "abnormality of the toe" (HP:0001776), it reflects a precise anatomical and morphological deviation within the broader category of toe abnormalities.  **Conclusion:**   The phenotype is a fixed, non-reducible flexion deformity of the fifth toe, with clear anatomical localization and structural specificity. It is distinct from other toe deformities and reflects a pathological change in joint mobility due to soft tissue shortening or fibrosis.
