ses with renal involvement.  **Conclusion:**   "Abnormal renal physiology" denotes a broad, functionally oriented phenotype indicating impaired kidney function, independent of structural changes. It serves as a high-level category in the HPO to group diverse functional disturbances, emphasizing the physiological rather than morphological aspects of renal disease.
