e, motor, or sensory function.   - **Clinical Relevance:** Often associated with severe neurodevelopmental delay, intellectual disability, seizures, and motor impairments. It may be part of a broader syndrome or occur in isolation.    **Conclusion:**   The concept refers specifically to a congenital structural defect involving the underdevelopment or absence of the cerebral white matter, with clear anatomical and developmental boundaries. It is distinct from acquired or non-cerebral white matter disorders and emphasizes the developmental origin and structural nature of the abnormality.
