ugh neuroimaging (MRI, CT) or histopathological examination.  **Conclusion:**   "Abnormal nervous system morphology" denotes a broad, non-specific phenotype characterized by structural abnormalities in the nervous system, without specifying the exact nature, location, or mechanism of the anomaly. It serves as a high-level term for capturing any deviation from normal anatomical form in neural tissues, primarily in developmental and congenital contexts.
