g., X-ray, MRI), where the epiphysis appears morphologically abnormal.  **Conclusion:**   This HPO concept refers to a specific, localized skeletal malformation involving the epiphysis of the proximal phalanx of the fifth toe, indicating abnormal development or structure of this bone end. It is a morphological phenotype with clear anatomical and developmental context, relevant to congenital or developmental disorders of the skeleton.
