ve T1" is a precise, quantitative imaging phenotype indicating abnormal myocardial tissue properties due to diffuse pathological changes, primarily reflecting interstitial remodeling or infiltration. It is a biomarker of myocardial disease with broad relevance in cardiomyopathies, infiltrative diseases, and early cardiac involvement in systemic conditions.
