rphological phenotype indicating a reduction in the physical thickness of an anatomical structure. It is non-specific regarding location or etiology but serves as a foundational term for describing structural underdevelopment, atrophy, or degeneration across multiple organ systems. Its meaning is best interpreted in conjunction with more specific child terms that define the affected structure.
